  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506575-Safeguarding Critical Minerals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our principal goal is for mining affected communities to mobilize and realize their rights and build citizen power; and for governments and mining companies to take meaningful action to safeguard human rights, prevent corruption, and equitably share economic benefits.  To achieve these goals, and in response to this political and influencing moment around critical energy transition minerals, we propose five pathways:

1. Provide frontline mining communities with political accompaniment and tools to realize their rights.
2. Strengthen mining industry governance and accountability, as well as gender-just revenue expenditure, by supporting national-levelcivil society and citizen campaigns
3. Advance stronger human rights due diligence, anti-corruption,and equity sharing in mineral value chains by developing US and global norms and frameworks.
4. Strengthen corporate polices and accountability on community rights, gender protections, and transparency
5. Build skills, share knowledge, and expand learning opportunities for Oxfam partners, allies, and decision-makers to increase advocacy impact</narrative>
  </description>
